@startuml 10-module-types
!include ../../../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/structural/component-diagram-style.iuml

title Types of Modules by Role

rectangle "**Functional**\nBusiness or application\nlogic that delivers\nsystem capabilities" as func $fill_primary

rectangle "**Data**\nData structures,\npersistence, and\nstorage concerns" as data $deep_primary

rectangle "**Infrastructure**\nCross-cutting technical\nservices: logging,\nsecurity, communication" as infra $fill_dynamic

rectangle "**Interface**\nInteraction with external\nentities: UIs, APIs,\nintegrations" as iface $deep_dynamic

rectangle "**Utility**\nCommon services and\nhelper functions used\nthroughout the system" as util $fill_ok

rectangle "**Facade**\nSimplified interface\nto complex subsystems,\nhiding internal structure" as facade $fill_caution

func -[hidden]right-> data
data -[hidden]right-> infra
infra -[hidden]right-> iface
iface -[hidden]right-> util
util -[hidden]right-> facade

note top of func
  Modules are categorized by the
  role they play within the system.
  A well-decomposed system typically
  includes several of these types.
end note

@enduml
